group: Td
formula: [CoCl4]^2-
construction: Fragment orbitals (extended Hückel)
headline: 
source: MO levels: UKS BP86, def2-SVP · 
note: Model: order and approximate spacing from extended Hückel (qualitative) · calculation in eV · not drawn: Cl4 internal: 7 levels, 14 e (4 core-like levels); tick Show all levels · electrons: Co 7, drawn 7; Cl4 32, drawn 18, Cl 3s core-like 4 levels 8 e, internal 3 levels 6 e; model and calculation: 25 drawn + 14 folded (7 levels, 4 core-like, 8 e) = 39 · labels in T<sub>d</sub>\n2 levels have an overlap below 0.80 with the matched calculated orbital
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (Co and Cl4). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments: above +0.02 bonding, below -0.02 antibonding (*), otherwise non-bonding. A bonding and an antibonding level of the same degeneracy that are the in-phase and out-of-phase combinations of the same fragment orbitals are joined as partners and share a colour; a level without such a partner keeps its own classification.\n\n**Scale.** The model columns show the order of the levels and their approximate spacing from extended Hückel, not a scale: close levels are drawn further apart so they can be read, and no model energy is printed (it is in the hover text). Extended Hückel antibonding energies are qualitative and typically far too high for short bonds to diffuse atoms such as B, Be and Al.\n\n**The calculation** is the column on the right, on its own energy axis in eV (not on the model's scale). For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, at its calculated energy, in the colour of the model level it matches. Beside each matched level, "overlap" is |<model MO|calculated MO>| (a number from 0 to 1); values below 0.80 are counted in the note under the diagram. Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\nVirtual orbitals above the LUMO depend strongly on the basis set.\n\n**Total electrons: 39** (Co 7, Cl4 32).\n\nEach model level carries a short grey tag naming the fragment orbitals it is mostly made of (shares of at least 20 %), such as Cr d or CO π*. Ligand-field view hides empty ligand-centred levels such as CO π*; transitions into them are charge transfer, not d–d.\n\nThe levels counted in the note under the diagram are model levels that sit almost entirely on the Cl4 and take no part in the interaction; they are counted, not drawn, in the calculation's column as well. The ns orbitals of a ligand atom that also has np (F 2s, Cl 3s) are treated as core-like here: the textbook sigma bonds are made of np.\n\n**Caveats.** 2 levels have an overlap below 0.80 with the matched calculated orbital. Extended Hückel puts empty antibonding orbitals tens of eV up, so an empty level more than 30 eV above the HOMO is drawn at the top of the diagram, marked with an up arrow, or not at all when it sits almost entirely on one fragment. A loose match means no calculated orbital resembles the model level closely; read its calculated energy with care.\n\n**Unrestricted calculation.** This is an unrestricted calculation: the levels are drawn at their alpha energies, and the beta electrons are matched to them by symmetry.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in Td (cross-checked against the code's own D2 labels, which agreed on all 103 orbitals both sides could label, and every computed label subduces to match).
verdict: differs The model puts 1e below 6t2, the model puts 2e* below 8t2*; the calculation has those the other way round (2 of 15 pairs of the 6 levels judged). The empty levels differ: the calculated LUMO is 9a1, the model's is 9t2*.
